          "r19"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "controls": "y",
    "capability_check": "y",
    "uncertainty_reported": "y",
    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing",
    "problems": "The study illustrates the approach on one AudioLLM and a representative decoder layer, and reports monosemanticity for selected top features rather than a prevalence estimate for individual neurons. The paper notes that the probing dataset is moderate in size.",
    "rows_left_out": "Human naming and semantic-similarity results (Table 2) evaluate concept-label quality, not neuron polysemanticity. Steering results (Table 3) measure an induced output shift, not the prevalence or coherence of neuron responses.",
    "untested": [
